PARITY reproduced from the web source (THE spec)
===========================================================================
  - Three-way Table / Compact / Comfortable selector as a WAI-ARIA radiogroup; controlled component —
    caller owns `value`, every change reported via `onChange` (the surface stores nothing).
  - DEFAULT_OPTIONS ['table','compact','comfortable'] + constrained `options` subset (web `options`).
  - onKeyDown: ArrowRight/ArrowLeft move + commit with wraparound; no-op when value ∉ options
    (web `if (idx < 0) return;`) — ported verbatim in DensityToggleProjector.next, unit-tested.
  - lucide ICONS → SF Symbols: Table2→tablecells, Rows3→rectangle.compress.vertical,
    Rows→rectangle.expand.vertical (distinct, density-semantic glyphs).
  - i18n: density.table/compact/comfortable + density.groupLabel ("List density"), ariaLabel override
    (web `ariaLabel ?? t('density.groupLabel')`) — all via the P1/S10 facade; no English literals in code.
  - Responsive label: web `hidden sm:inline` → labels collapse to icon-only on a compact horizontal size
    class (iOS), shown otherwise (macOS always shows). Guarded `#if os(iOS)` like sibling surfaces.
  - selected → raised surface fill + primary text (web `bg-[var(--surface-2)] text-primary`);
    unselected → secondary text on clear (web `text-secondary`); focus ring (web `ring-2`) on the track.
  - testId → accessibility identifiers (group = testId|slug, segment = `{group}-{density}`, web
    `${testId}-${opt}`).

  REAL states reproduced (faithful-parity note): the web <DensityToggle> is a PURE, CONTROLLED
  presentational component — only hook is useTranslation, no fetch / React-Query / Promise — so it has NO
  loading / error / stale / offline branch. Inventing such chrome would FABRICATE states the source does
  not have (same reasoning as the accepted sibling presentational primitives ActiveFilterChips-0147,
  InlineCallout-0124, Delta-0081, MetricCard-0095). Reproduced branches: populated radiogroup (default +
  constrained), per-option selected/unselected, value-not-in-options arrow no-op, custom-vs-default group
  label, and the degenerate empty-options case (a friendly labelled empty-state view — HIG: never a blank
  box), plus VoiceOver / Dynamic Type / Reduce-Motion.

